WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.335
- Hello, I'm Gav.
- I'm Dan.

00:00:02.368 --> 00:00:04.470 align:start position:0%
Welcome to
the "The Super Slow Show."

00:00:04.503 --> 00:00:06.406
- We're at the drop zone.
- Yes, we are.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:07.774 align:start position:0%
That means we're
about to drop something.

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:09.442 align:start size:81% position:19%
It might just be this car.

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:11.611
Yeah, this is from
the catapult video.

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:13.246 align:end position:100%
Right.
We couldn't sell it,

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:15.481 align:end position:100%
and we thought it's not
sufficiently trashed enough.

00:00:15.514 --> 00:00:16.749 align:start position:0%
We definitely
dented it up.

00:00:16.782 --> 00:00:18.418
- Yeah.
- But it's not annihilated.

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:19.519 align:end position:100%
It's not
completely crushed.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:24.190
Dan: <i> Oh! </i>
Gav: <i> Right through the zero.</i>

00:00:24.223 --> 00:00:28.161
- <i> Oh, God! </i>
- <i> That was so clean.</i>

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.229 align:end position:100%
So we've got
a 40-ton crane,

00:00:30.262 --> 00:00:32.365 align:end position:100%
and we're gonna lift it
about 80 feet up into the air.

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:34.200
Wonder what speed
it's gonna go when
it hits the floor.

00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:35.268 align:start position:0%
That is up there.

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:36.636 align:start size:41% position:59%
It really is.

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.237 align:start position:0%
We're going to be getting
this on two Phantoms,

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:39.739
one that's wide,
a thousand frames,

00:00:39.772 --> 00:00:41.741
one a little bit tighter,
2,000 frames a second.

00:00:41.774 --> 00:00:44.143 align:start position:0%
We've also got a GoPro
in the back,

00:00:44.176 --> 00:00:45.545 align:start position:0%
looking forwards.

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:48.714 align:start position:0%
And another one
on this fat hook.

00:00:48.747 --> 00:00:50.483 align:end position:100%
This is the biggest hook
I've ever seen.

00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:51.784
- It's massive.
- Massive.

00:00:51.817 --> 00:00:53.519 align:start position:0%
We also thought
that an impact into the dirt

00:00:53.552 --> 00:00:54.654 align:start size:97% position:3%
would be too soft,

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.322 size:84% position:42%
so we've replaced the floor

00:00:56.355 --> 00:00:58.491
with, like, an inch of steel.

00:00:58.524 --> 00:01:01.260
So this should be horrendous.

00:01:01.293 --> 00:01:03.363
<i> ( theme music playing )</i>

00:01:10.636 --> 00:01:12.672
( crane whirring )

00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:19.479 align:start position:0%
Well, it's definitely something
we couldn't do in your back
garden, for sure.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.247
Absolutely not.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.849
That crane just lifted it
like it was nothing.

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:24.350
It's like, all right,
here we go, 80 feet.

00:01:24.383 --> 00:01:27.520
It's absolutely dwarfed
the ruler.

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:29.122 align:end position:100%
Imagine being
in the front seat,

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:31.124 align:start size:75% position:25%
how scary that would be.

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.326
- You wouldn't live.
  There's no way.
- No, there's no way.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:34.494
- All right.
- Although, I reckon

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:36.195 align:start size:56% position:44%
that when it hits,

00:01:36.228 --> 00:01:38.498 align:end position:100%
the car's going to come
forwards towards the Phantom

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.399
- because of the way it is.
- All right.

00:01:40.432 --> 00:01:41.701 align:end position:100%
I'm really looking
forward to this.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:42.902
- You wanna get it going?
- I'm ready.

00:01:42.935 --> 00:01:46.539 align:end position:100%
All right.
Three! Two! One! Drop!

00:01:46.572 --> 00:01:48.307
Oh! Oh!

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.443
( laughing )

00:01:55.414 --> 00:01:58.184
That was just
a little bounce.

00:01:58.217 --> 00:02:01.554 align:start position:0%
Yeah.
At one point it hit the floor.
I think it was in mid-air again.

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:03.156
Gav: I think,
if there's an area,

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:04.757
where it's, like,
back off the ground again.

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:06.792
Wow. Oh, we smashed
the windows, though.
We got more points.

00:02:06.825 --> 00:02:07.927 size:88% position:44%
Should we go check it out?

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.795 align:start size:34% position:66%
Yeah.

00:02:09.828 --> 00:02:12.198
- Oh.
- Look at this.

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:15.268 align:start position:0%
- ( gasps )
- You can still see the
 100-point marks on the window.

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:17.203 align:start size:69% position:31%
It fell out perfectly.

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:18.738 align:start size:78% position:22%
Look, it's just laid out,

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:20.406 align:end position:100%
Dan:
And the GoPro's still
attached to it.

00:02:20.439 --> 00:02:23.576 align:end position:100%
I think the only way
you could've done that

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:25.411 align:start size:56% position:44%
is to drop a car
from a crane.

00:02:25.444 --> 00:02:27.547 align:start position:0%
I think you're right.
I absolutely think you're right.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.415 align:start position:0%
Gav:
Oh, that is a flat front.

00:02:29.448 --> 00:02:31.250 align:end position:100%
Dan:
Oh, man, that is squished.

00:02:31.283 --> 00:02:33.186 align:end position:100%
'Cause that's not like hitting
a car, where it's uneven.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:34.253 align:end position:100%
That just absolutely
crushed it.

00:02:34.286 --> 00:02:35.821 align:start size:97% position:3%
Oh, man.

00:02:35.854 --> 00:02:39.625
Sound guy's definitely not
gonna be pleased this time.

00:02:39.658 --> 00:02:41.827 align:start position:0%
I mean, at least last time
you could drive it afterwards.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:44.197
This, I think,
is unsalvageable.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.365 align:end position:100%
I'd just say
it's more breezy.

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:49.902 align:start position:0% line:0%
Gav: <i> Crunch.</i>

00:02:49.935 --> 00:02:52.505 align:end position:100% line:0%
Dan: <i> Oh, look at the ripple
 go all along the...</i>

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:54.540 align:start position:0% line:0%
<i>It just drives
into itself.</i>

00:02:54.573 --> 00:02:56.576 align:start position:0% line:0%
<i>Look at the dust
it kicked out
from the front.</i>

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:58.978 align:start position:0% line:0%
<i>It's, like, wafted
all the dust away.</i>

00:02:59.011 --> 00:03:00.913 align:start position:0% line:0%
<i>Oh, look, the mirror.</i>

00:03:00.946 --> 00:03:03.649 align:start position:0%
<i>The million points
has gone flying.</i>

00:03:03.682 --> 00:03:06.319 size:78% position:39%
<i>You can see one mirror...</i>

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:07.687 align:start size:69% position:31%
<i> What are the chances?</i>

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:18.364
- Dan: <i> Oh, close-up. </i>
- Gav: <i> This is satisfying.</i>

00:03:19.665 --> 00:03:21.567 align:start size:59% position:41% line:0%
<i> Glad we got
 that metal there.</i>

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:23.336 line:0%
- <i> Yeah, that's solid. </i>
- <i> That tin-foil effect again.</i>

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:25.404 line:0%
- <i> On the hard metal. </i>
- <i> Oh, look.</i>

00:03:25.437 --> 00:03:28.341
- <i> The mirror hit the car
 and then flung out </i>
- <i> It popped out.</i>

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:30.577
- <i> Yeah. </i>
- <i> It was like a catapult.</i>

00:03:32.511 --> 00:03:33.512 align:start position:0%
<i>That's amazing.</i>

00:03:33.545 --> 00:03:34.647 align:start size:63% position:38%
So then it took off.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:35.848 align:start size:78% position:22%
How high did it even get?

00:03:35.881 --> 00:03:37.483 align:end position:100%
It must've been,
like, an inch.

00:03:37.516 --> 00:03:38.884 align:start size:97% position:3%
That's--

00:03:38.917 --> 00:03:40.586 align:start position:0%
I like that I'm leaning down
to try and see under.

00:03:40.619 --> 00:03:43.256 align:end position:100%
Yeah, I did the same.
You beat me there.

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:44.390 align:start position:0%
Nope, that's
completely useless.

00:03:44.423 --> 00:03:45.491
Idiots.

00:03:51.563 --> 00:03:53.266 align:start position:0%
<i>Oh, we get to see
the window smash.</i>

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:55.268 align:start position:0%
<i>See, there's
the side door.</i>

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:59.305
- <i> See? </i>
- <i> Yeah, the side
 smashed off as well.</i>

00:03:59.338 --> 00:04:01.874 align:start size:91% position:9%
- <i> Lovely. </i>
- <i> So I think we should
 destroy it even more.</i>

00:04:01.907 --> 00:04:03.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
- <i> All right. </i>
- <i> All right,
 should we flip it over?</i>

00:04:03.742 --> 00:04:06.579
Yeah, let's flip it over and
we'll destroy it some more.

00:04:06.612 --> 00:04:08.414
If you could open the doors,
which you can't,

00:04:08.447 --> 00:04:10.916
there's also enough room
to actually sit in there.

00:04:10.949 --> 00:04:12.718
- That's not good enough.
- That's not good enough.

00:04:12.751 --> 00:04:14.687 align:start position:0%
- Definitely not good enough.
- I think we should change that.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.055 size:88% position:44%
What have you got in mind?

00:04:16.088 --> 00:04:19.325 align:end position:100%
Ta-da. This guy
is a concrete K-rail,

00:04:19.358 --> 00:04:20.660 align:end position:100%
weighs about
3 1/2 metric tons,

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:21.927 align:start size:50% position:50%
in English, so--

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:23.562 size:81% position:41%
What's that in American?

00:04:23.595 --> 00:04:24.797 align:start size:59% position:41%
About 8,000 pounds.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:26.532 size:88% position:44%
Ooh, what's that in stone?

00:04:26.565 --> 00:04:29.869 line:0%
- Wait, 8,000 divided by 14.
- We haven't got time for this.

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:33.306
- Yeah.
- So, I think drop it
  on the roof lengthways,

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:35.341
and see how much carnage
we can cause,

00:04:35.374 --> 00:04:36.842
'cause I wanna completely
finish this thing off.

00:04:36.875 --> 00:04:38.010
- All right.
- Yeah?

00:04:38.043 --> 00:04:39.646
- Let's hoist 'er up.
- Cool.

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:46.952 align:end position:100%
So you don't often see
a roof-on collision, do you?

00:04:46.985 --> 00:04:49.989 align:end position:100%
It's either a head-on or
a fender bender or a side--

00:04:50.022 --> 00:04:52.792 align:start position:0%
So this is simulating
a plane nose-diving

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:54.460 align:start position:0%
into the roof of a car.

00:04:54.493 --> 00:04:55.828 align:end position:100%
With a concrete block on it
for some reason.

00:04:55.861 --> 00:04:57.797
- Yeah.
- Yeah. You ready?

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.398 align:start position:0%
Let's turn this thing
into a pancake.

00:04:59.431 --> 00:05:00.933
- Dan: Cool.
- Or a hot dog.

00:05:00.966 --> 00:05:03.036 align:start size:69% position:31%
Three, two, one, drop!

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:11.811
- Oh...
- That is beefy.

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:14.847 align:start size:63% position:38%
The deep bassy thud.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:17.850 align:start size:78% position:22%
That has smushed the car.

00:05:17.883 --> 00:05:19.452 align:start size:75% position:25%
Can you hear it hissing?

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:20.753 align:start position:0%
Should we get in there?

00:05:20.786 --> 00:05:22.021
- Yeah.
- Let's check it out.

00:05:22.054 --> 00:05:26.125
Ah, the delicious hiss
of the Freon.

00:05:26.158 --> 00:05:28.394 align:start size:25% position:75%
Oh, man.

00:05:28.427 --> 00:05:30.429 align:end position:100%
You would have to get
into some serious trouble

00:05:30.462 --> 00:05:31.798 align:end position:100%
for your car
to look like that.

00:05:33.432 --> 00:05:35.701 align:start position:0%
I mean, it's certainly
popped the tires.

00:05:35.734 --> 00:05:38.404
- It popped all the tires.
- I'm not sure if they were
 already popped.

00:05:38.437 --> 00:05:40.439
I don't think
I've ever seen a car

00:05:40.472 --> 00:05:42.908 align:start position:0%
more annihilated
than this,

00:05:42.941 --> 00:05:45.511 align:start position:0%
unless you're talking
like that's been crushed
at a scrappy.

00:05:45.544 --> 00:05:46.746 align:start size:72% position:28%
Yeah, one that's cubed.

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:49.148 align:start position:0%
Yeah, this is the most
crushed and smushed

00:05:49.181 --> 00:05:50.950 align:start position:0%
a car has ever been
that I've seen.

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:52.785 align:start size:34% position:66%
Almost sad.

00:05:52.818 --> 00:05:55.087 align:start position:0%
Sound guy will be sad.
That's for sure.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.789
All right, let's go
look at the footage.

00:05:56.822 --> 00:05:57.990 align:start size:78% position:22%
That just looks so wrong.

00:05:58.023 --> 00:05:59.725 align:start position:0%
It's going so fast.

00:05:59.758 --> 00:06:01.761 align:end position:100%
A concrete rail should not be
in the air like that.

00:06:22.214 --> 00:06:25.484
- Dan: <i> Whoa. </i>
- Gav: <i> You see all the dust
 get kicked up?</i>

00:06:25.517 --> 00:06:27.052
Dan: <i> Oh, man.</i>

00:06:27.085 --> 00:06:30.423
<i> All the tires popped.
 Everything just smushed.</i>

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:33.459 align:start position:0%
Gav: <i> Even the air being forced
out through the windows</i>

00:06:33.492 --> 00:06:35.661 align:start position:0%
<i>is significant,
like you see, like a... 
( imitates air whooshing )</i>

00:06:35.694 --> 00:06:40.533
<i> That car probably weighs a
metric ton and a half, maybe.</i>

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:43.135
<i>That K-rail is more than twice
 the weight of the car,</i>

00:06:43.168 --> 00:06:46.705
<i> a much smaller surface area.</i>

00:06:46.738 --> 00:06:50.843 align:start position:0%
And then you can see--
because obviously the engine
is the hardest part.

00:06:50.876 --> 00:06:53.579 align:start position:0%
The other end, the back end,
went all the way down.

00:06:53.612 --> 00:06:55.714 align:start size:88% position:13%
Any air that was
in the car

00:06:55.747 --> 00:06:57.516
is now out and gone.

00:06:57.549 --> 00:06:59.152
Like, there's
no space in there.

00:07:00.986 --> 00:07:03.189 align:start position:0%
That's beautiful
and horrific.

00:07:06.892 --> 00:07:08.828 align:end position:100%
Some people pay a lot of money
to lower their cars.

00:07:08.861 --> 00:07:10.229 size:88% position:56%
All you need to do is drop
a concrete block on it.

00:07:10.262 --> 00:07:11.630
- Yeah.
- Look at it.

00:07:11.663 --> 00:07:12.998 align:start position:0%
I mean, you say that
like this was cheap,

00:07:13.031 --> 00:07:14.099 align:start position:0%
like this was
the cheap version.

00:07:14.132 --> 00:07:15.468
Good point.

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:16.635 align:start position:0%
Way more expensive
to do it like this.

00:07:16.668 --> 00:07:18.003
Fair enough, yeah.

00:07:18.036 --> 00:07:20.673 align:start position:0%
Hopefully you enjoyed
that mindless destruction.

